PN,38702
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1786110488
OL,3,CPedal power! Artist relies on public
OL,4,Cto live-stitch Brighton's Royal
OL,5,CPavilion
OL,7,FHowever, bringing the artwork to life
OL,8,Fhas relied on help from the public.
OL,9,FThe sewing machine drew its
OL,10,Felectricity from volunteers hopping
OL,11,Fonto a specially adapted stationary
OL,12,Fbike.
OL,14,F"I used a sewing machine to stitch the
OL,15,FRoyal Pavilion from life with pedal
OL,16,Fpower," Harriet explained. "People
OL,17,Ffrom the public rode the bike to power
OL,18,Fthe sewing machine, and that allowed
OL,19,Fme to draw what I could see."
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38703
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1786110488
OL,3,CPedal power! Artist relies on public
OL,4,Cto live-stitch Brighton's Royal
OL,5,CPavilion
OL,7,FIf cyclists pedalled too fast or too
OL,8,Fslow, the sewing machine responded
OL,9,Finstantly, creating a dynamic,
OL,10,Finteractive atmosphere for spectators,
OL,11,Ftourists, and local residents.
OL,13,FHarriet developed the setup after
OL,14,Flooking for ways to work without
OL,15,Felectricity outdoors.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G3/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38704
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1786110488
OL,3,CPedal power! Artist relies on public
OL,4,Cto live-stitch Brighton's Royal
OL,5,CPavilion
OL,7,F"I was always looking for a plug, a
OL,8,Ftable, and a chair," she said. "I
OL,9,Frealised I could use batteries, but
OL,10,Fthey would run out. The bicycle added
OL,11,Fto the collaborative feel and meant I
OL,12,Fcould stitch anywhere I wanted to.
OL,14,F"I've been all around the world
OL,15,Fstitching on streets, mountains, and
OL,16,Fin jungles."
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38705
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1786110488
OL,3,CPedal power! Artist relies on public
OL,4,Cto live-stitch Brighton's Royal
OL,5,CPavilion
OL,7,FSpeaking on the impact of having the
OL,8,Fpublic drive the artwork, Harriet
OL,9,Fadded: "Their energy makes the art
OL,10,Fpossible. I love the participation -
OL,11,Fit draws the audience in so they feel
OL,12,Fa part of the art."
OL,14,F"I've spent years setting up my
OL,15,Fmachine in all sorts of places, and
OL,16,Fthe magic always happens through the
OL,17,Fconversations.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
